// 5:3, three equal bars. The flower is the Commons drawing's, centered on the flag and 288.9 by 298.5 of 1600 by 960,
// which is 0.9028 by 0.9328 of the 5 by 3.
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Sapphic Flag, Simplified Violets"
  designer "lesbeux-moved"
  designer "lesbeux-moved"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "LicenseRef-Public-Domain"
  adapted-from "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sapphic_Flag_alternate_with_violet.svg" {
    author "Opensofias (an autotrace of the Pride-Flags DeviantArt image; Commons credits Cayla / lexbeux-moved)"
    license "LicenseRef-Public-Domain"
    part "the violet"
  }
  date "2016-09"
  series "sapphic"
  version "simplified-violet"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20210329002721/https://www.deviantart.com/pride-flags/art/Sapphic-2-629060222"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20181217213955/https://pride-color-schemes.tumblr.com/post/162230388064/sapphic"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20250606032425/https://lesbeux-moved.tumblr.com/post/126717498095/sapphic-wlw-sga-women-flag-pink-love-violets"
  source "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sapphic_Flag_alternate_with_violet.svg"
  note "The original flag was posted on 14 August 2015 by the Tumblr user lesbeux-moved (Wayback Machine, 6 June 2025). It has pink, very light lavender and pink stripes with an illustration of two violets. Its post says pink is for love and the violets, and the lavender-ish color, recall women giving violets to women they were wooing. The post's image is 296 by 166 pixels with colors #ff88a9 and #fbf2ff."
  note "The simplification is attributed to Mod Hermy of the Tumblr blog pride-color-schemes, which couldn't be confirmed."
  note "Commons marks the violet's copyright status as disputed, and as a simple shape not eligible for copyright. Its license here follows Commons, and should be checked before relying on it."
  note "This file is the simplified version. Its earliest publication read is 'Sapphic (2)' by Pride-Flags on DeviantArt, published 11 September 2016 (Wayback Machine, 29 March 2021): 'Designed by: lesbeux-moved', and a note that it simplifies the earlier design because the poster couldn't redraw its detailed flower. An undated edit there says its colors were changed to be more like the other sapphic flags. Its 5000 by 3000 pixel image has stripes of 1000, colors #fd8ba8 and #fbf2ff, and the flower centered, 0.90 by 0.93 of the 3-unit height. A post of 25 June 2017 on the Tumblr blog pride-color-schemes, credited to lesbeux-moved with the simplification by Mod Hermy, shows three equal stripes and a simplified five-petaled violet with a small pink and yellow center. Its image is 500 by 300 pixels with colors #fd8ba8 and #fbf2ff, which match the Commons drawing. The original's two-violet illustration is a raster picture, and isn't encoded."
  note "The violet's drawing is from Commons, used unchanged. Its history says Opensofias autotraced it in 2020 from the DeviantArt image, which it names as its source, and it matches that image's flower. Its petals are #c76bc5, its ring #f996c9 and its center #fff71e. The post's image shows a violet, and doesn't give these values."
  note "No post states a proportion. The 5:3 proportion and the equal stripes are the DeviantArt image's and the 2017 image's (500 by 300 pixels, stripes of 100). The date is the DeviantArt post's month; the colors here may date from its later, undated edit, and are those of the 2017 post. Whether Mod Hermy is the Pride-Flags poster isn't shown by either source."
}
palette {
  pink "#fd8ba8"
  lavender "#fbf2ff"
}
proportion hoist=3 fly=5

bars pink lavender pink

charge svg {
  at center
  fly 0.9028
  hoist 0.9328
  markup #"""
